Local OpenWrt packages paired with the driver snapshot in ../pon-drivers/UPSTREAM.
The PON board data scripts and identity-image helper are split out of the
upstream luci-app-pon into airoha-pon-board-data. The local LuCI package depends
on that package and airoha-pon-debug.

The normal packages feed still supplies the Rust build helpers, and the LuCI
feed supplies luci.mk. No separate PON feed update or installation is needed.

Local mode-selection fix: ponctl exposes the effective kernel line mode, and
airoha-pond resolves an empty UCI mode before bringing up its control interface.
The active mode takes precedence over a pending configuration. These changes
are additional to the recorded upstream snapshot.
